<Project>

  <!-- The same file, reached as an MSBuild project SDK rather than as a package
       reference. The difference is *when*: an SDK is resolved from NuGet before the
       project is evaluated, so a property it defines can be read by the project
       body. A package reference cannot do that — its props arrive through
       {project}.nuget.g.props, which does not exist until restore has run, and
       restore needs TargetFrameworks to decide what to restore.

       That is not a preference. A named target-framework set delivered by a package
       reference evaluates to empty, and NuGet reports `Invalid framework
       identifier ''`. Anything a project reads at evaluation time has to arrive
       this way. -->
  <Import Project="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../build/Rinzler78.Build.props" />

</Project>
